-- Ekwo OS — Pakistan: chart of accounts, journals, taxes and defaults.
--
-- Generated from packs/pk at version 0.1.0, do not edit.
-- Change the pack and run `ekwo pack build pk`; `ekwo pack check --all`
-- refuses a seed that is not the exact output of its pack, and the CI runs it.
--
-- Community pack — not reviewed.
-- Written from:
--   Sales Tax Act, 1990, as amended up to 30 June 2026 (the Finance Act, 2026 amendments shown in red) — s. 2(9) due date, s. 2(43) tax period, s. 3(1) the 18 per cent rate and s. 3(1A) the 4 per cent further tax, s. 4 and the Fifth Schedule (zero rating), s. 6 (time and manner of payment), s. 7 and 8 (input tax, tax credit not allowed), s. 8B (adjustable input tax), s. 13 and the Sixth Schedule (exemption), s. 21(2) (suspension of registration), s. 23 (tax invoices and integration), s. 26 (return), the Eighth Schedule (reduced rates) and the Eleventh Schedule (withholding) (Federal Board of Revenue)
--     https://download1.fbr.gov.pk/Docs/20267171373418951SalesTaxAct1990updatedupto30.06.2026.pdf
--   Finance Act, 2026, published in the Gazette of Pakistan, Extraordinary, on 26 June 2026 (Federal Board of Revenue)
--     https://download1.fbr.gov.pk/Docs/20266291261044366FinanceAct2026.pdf
--   Sales Tax Rules, 2006, updated up to 6 August 2025 — rule 14 and form STR-7 (Sales Tax and Federal Excise Return), rule 18 (electronic filing of the return, payment by the 15th and filing by the 18th), Annexures A, C and I, Chapter XIV (rules 150Q onwards, electronic invoicing and integration) (Federal Board of Revenue)
--     https://download1.fbr.gov.pk/Docs/2025881385446623STR-2006-UpdatedUpto06-08-2025(ver-iv).pdf
--   Sales tax due dates — the monthly return, Annexure C filed on the 10th, payment on the 15th and the return e-filed by the 18th of the month following the period (Federal Board of Revenue)
--     https://www.fbr.gov.pk/sales-tax-due-dates/51148/101162
--   File sales tax return — the Federal Board of Revenue page on the monthly sales tax return (Federal Board of Revenue)
--     https://www.fbr.gov.pk/categ/file-sales-tax-return/51148/50849/101159
--   FBR IRIS — the portal where the monthly sales tax return is filed and the tax paid, and where invoices are reported (Federal Board of Revenue)
--     https://iris.fbr.gov.pk
--   Circular No. 01 of 2023 — Finance (Supplementary) Act, 2023, explanation of important amendments in the Sales Tax Act, 1990: the standard rate increased from 17 per cent to 18 per cent (Federal Board of Revenue)
--     https://download1.fbr.gov.pk/Docs/20232281524459451Circular01-2023SalesTaxFederalExcise.pdf
--   The Punjab Sales Tax on Services Act, 2012 — section 2(41A) standard rate of sixteen percent and the Second Schedule (not opened from the place the pack was written; see the README) (Government of the Punjab)
--     https://punjablaws.gov.pk/laws/2506.html
--   The Sindh Sales Tax on Services Act, 2011, as amended up to the Sindh Finance Act, 2025 — section 8(1) standard rate of fifteen per cent, section 2(36) due date, section 30 return, Second Schedule (Sindh Revenue Board)
--     https://www.srb.gos.pk/srb/wp-content/uploads/2026/01/Sindh-Sales-Tax-Act-2011-25-26-2.pdf
--   The Khyber Pakhtunkhwa Sales Tax on Services Act, 2022 (Act No. XIX of 2022), updated with the Khyber Pakhtunkhwa Finance Act, 2024 — section 2(x) due dates, section 9(1) standard rate of fifteen percent (Khyber Pakhtunkhwa Revenue Authority)
--     https://kpra.gov.pk/wp-content/uploads/2024/07/KP-STS-ACT-2022-Updated-2024.pdf
--   The Balochistan Sales Tax on Services Act, 2015 (Act VI of 2015) — section 1(3) commencement on 1 July 2015, section 2(18) due date, Second Schedule at fifteen per cent (Provincial Assembly of Balochistan)
--     https://pabalochistan.gov.pk/storage/3965/2018-10-23-12_48_35balochistan-sales-tax-act-2015.pdf
--   Islamabad Capital Territory (Tax on Services) Ordinance, 2001, updated up to 30 June 2025 — section 3 and the Schedule, Table-1 at fifteen percent (Federal Board of Revenue)
--     https://download1.fbr.gov.pk/Docs/2025711172945966ICTOUpdatedupto30.06.2025.pdf
--   Companies Act, 2017 — the Third Schedule (reporting frameworks by class of company) and the Fourth and Fifth Schedules (preparation of financial statements), as published by the Securities and Exchange Commission of Pakistan (Securities and Exchange Commission of Pakistan)
--     https://www.secp.gov.pk/document/3rd-4th-and-5th-schedule-to-the-companies-act-2017/
--   Use of IFRS Standards by jurisdiction — Pakistan: full IFRS for listed, public interest and large-sized companies, IFRS for SMEs for medium-sized companies and the Revised AFRS for small-sized entities (IFRS Foundation)
--     https://www.ifrs.org/use-around-the-world/use-of-ifrs-standards-by-jurisdiction/view-jurisdiction/pakistan/
--
-- Reference data: `install_country_template()` copies it into a company,
-- nothing here belongs to a company.

